{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y17YiVLQWnLmLVJvxXdufh","type":"tool_result","content":"0a355a9 ard(triage:engineer): #357 Adds a transient error class to gitx, a separate bounded backoff retry… [skip ci]\n4848243 ard(triage:engineer): #323 Adds a no-commit merge helper to gitx, a merge-parent option with guard… [skip ci]\n7ad60bb ard(triage:lead): #205 The blocker is gone: the local ard-agent image (#243) and the default i… [skip ci]\nc332d77 feat: Default ard-agent image and role image builds, part 55b: d… (#351)\n220076f feat: Default ard-agent image and role image builds, part 55a: l… (#243) (#324)\n370b31b ard(worker:engineer): #243 The Dockerfile needs the vendor's real SHA-256 checksums for the pinned… [skip ci]\n2f922be feat: Scanner: missing-tests, part 2: scan, Dockerfile and start… (#285)\n0f0d825 ard(triage:engineer): #243 Adds a locally built agent image (Dockerfile and test script under depl… [skip ci]\n95067de ard(triage:lead): #243 Adds a locally built default agent image: a Dockerfile and test script… [skip ci]\ned1e9dc ard(triage:engineer): #213 Adds the missing-tests scan script and pinned Dockerfile, embeds them a… [skip ci]\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go\ninternal/servecmd/cfgloader_test.go\ninternal/gitx/export_test.go\ninternal/config/render.go\ninternal/config/types.go\ninternal/config/load_test.go\ninternal/config/discover.go\ninternal/configcmd/config_test.go\ninternal/roles/eng_review_test.go\ninternal/roles/license_review_test.go\n379:3. **Run the aid, then the agent.** After the pin, a role with an executable `aid` in its directory (reviewers only, like a scanner's `scan`; #205) has it run by the controller as its own executor job at the pinned head, before the agent, so the findings of its deterministic tools do not depend on the host or on the agent choosing to run them. The tool finds; the agent explains, ranks and confirms. The aid job is read-only, has no `Env` and no `Fixed` entries (no model credential, no GitHub token), runs with `--network none` under Docker (a role `Dockerfile` or `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`; known CVEs stay with the `cve` scanner, so the aid never queries vulnerability databases), and has its own timeout of 5 minutes (shorter if the role's is), counted inside the review job's timeout: the agent gets what is left, at least one minute. Its inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/changed.txt` (one path per line, `.ard/<issue#>/` left out) and `diff.patch`. Its output is JSONL on stdout, one object per result with exactly `tool`, `rule`, `file`, `line`, `severity` (`critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`) and `message`, capped at 256 KiB (more is a failure). ard validates it: a line that is not JSON, has an unknown key, a bad tool, rule, severity or line, or a path that is absolute, has `..` or is not in `changed.txt` is dropped and counted; a message is redacted, cut at 1 KiB and secret-scanned like a log, and a line that still trips the scanner is dropped. Matched text is never kept: the aid must print rule ids and positions only. The result is written to `.ard-input/<issue#>/aid.jsonl` and is the first of the agent's untrusted inputs; the starter prompt reads it first and runs the tools itself only when the file is absent. **Failure:** a failed, timed-out or invalid aid (any dropped line counts as invalid) never stops the review. The input says the aid failed and why, and close-out turns an `approve` into `changes` with a note. **Blocking:** a `gitleaks` result on a line the PR added becomes a blocking `high` finding with a `[secret]` message that ard adds to the review in code (carrying the rule id only); the agent cannot drop it, and an `approve` becomes `changes`. gosec and semgrep results stay advisory. Both rules apply only to roles that have an `aid`. **Host mode:** with no role `Dockerfile` and no `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`, the aid runs on the host, as ard-owned code that reads but never executes PR code; its environment holds no credential, but nothing enforces its network, and it runs as the controller's uid without a sandbox: the residual risk of #84 applies to it too. The starter `security-review/aid` pins gosec, gitleaks and semgrep (vendored local rules, `--metrics=off`, `--disable-nosem`) in the role's `Dockerfile`, built on the default ard-agent image (k8s role images stay with #245). Then **run the agent** with `.ard/reviewers/<role>/prompt.txt` and these untrusted inputs: `.ard-input/<issue#>/diff.patch` (the controller's diff from the merge base with `main` to the pinned head, `--stat` then the patch, taken with `--text`, `--no-textconv` and attributes read from the empty tree so a `.gitattributes` entry cannot hide a change, with this issue's `.ard/<issue#>/` left out and cut at 1 MiB), `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md` and `comments.md` (written by the loop, never committed), the committed `.ard/<issue#>/` (plan, triage and worker role files and logs) and the sidecar (security policy, license allowlist). The loop runs every git command against the controller clone, never in the reviewer's worktree (the agent itself may run read-only git there). In a later round it also gets `.ard-input/<issue#>/previous-review.md`, its own earlier report, read from the pinned head, and says which findings are resolved.\n575:- **Image pins for the Kubernetes executor.** The deploy job pins the agent image's digest beside the ard image's in the deployment repository: `deploy/argocd` takes `agentImage: {repository, digest}` and passes it to each child, and with `executor.kind: k8s` `deploy/charts/ard-serve` renders `ARD_K8S_AGENT_IMAGE=<repository>@<digest>` and `ARD_K8S_POD_IMAGE=<ard image>@<digest>` (`pre` and `post` run the ard image). Both values are digest placeholders (`digest: \"\"`) in this repository; with executor k8s an empty or malformed agent digest, or a tag in the repository, is refused, and executor local renders no `ARD_K8S_*` env. To fill them, the deploy job reads each pushed digest (`docker buildx imagetools inspect ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard/agent:sha-<7> --format '{{json .Manifest.Digest}}'`), verifies the signature and revision label as for the ard image, and writes `agentImage.digest` in the same commit as `image.digest`. No `imagePullSecrets`: both images are public.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a35fa2b5-d93b-4d8a-8dfa-4624f696edc9","uuid":"b9fa99cf-d68b-4e83-b2c0-681af1277093","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:46:59.370Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"0a355a9 ard(triage:engineer): #357 Adds a transient error class to gitx, a separate bounded backoff retry… [skip ci]\n4848243 ard(triage:engineer): #323 Adds a no-commit merge helper to gitx, a merge-parent option with guard… [skip ci]\n7ad60bb ard(triage:lead): #205 The blocker is gone: the local ard-agent image (#243) and the default i… [skip ci]\nc332d77 feat: Default ard-agent image and role image builds, part 55b: d… (#351)\n220076f feat: Default ard-agent image and role image builds, part 55a: l… (#243) (#324)\n370b31b ard(worker:engineer): #243 The Dockerfile needs the vendor's real SHA-256 checksums for the pinned… [skip ci]\n2f922be feat: Scanner: missing-tests, part 2: scan, Dockerfile and start… (#285)\n0f0d825 ard(triage:engineer): #243 Adds a locally built agent image (Dockerfile and test script under depl… [skip ci]\n95067de ard(triage:lead): #243 Adds a locally built default agent image: a Dockerfile and test script… [skip ci]\ned1e9dc ard(triage:engineer): #213 Adds the missing-tests scan script and pinned Dockerfile, embeds them a… [skip ci]\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go\ninternal/servecmd/cfgloader_test.go\ninternal/gitx/export_test.go\ninternal/config/render.go\ninternal/config/types.go\ninternal/config/load_test.go\ninternal/config/discover.go\ninternal/configcmd/config_test.go\ninternal/roles/eng_review_test.go\ninternal/roles/license_review_test.go\n379:3. **Run the aid, then the agent.** After the pin, a role with an executable `aid` in its directory (reviewers o