{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQJTm5EcMnV2baYLFZbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X5gnmjKEfWcLXnpiWZiwhT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/work/.ard/245/triage-lead.md","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis is the last slice of the default agent image work. It lets roles that ship their own Dockerfile run under the Kubernetes executor by building those images and making them pullable by the cluster. Both dependencies appear to have landed on main: the local ard-agent image (part 55a) and the Kubernetes executor series, including its agent and pod images and image pins. So the work can start, and the engineer plans it.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: choose how role images build on the published agent image instead of the local-only one, where they are built and pushed, how the k8s executor picks the image for each role, and the tests and proposal update.\n- worker engineer: executor, build and docs changes, with tests.\n\n## Open issues\n- The repository has no architect triage role, so the engineer's plan has to make the design choices itself. These are: the base image for role images on the cluster path, the registry and whether it is public, and whether role images are built in CI and pinned by digest or built at runtime. A maintainer should check these choices in the plan before the worker starts.\n- The change will probably touch Jenkinsfile, Dockerfile or deploy/. Those are protected paths, so the pull request will wait for a human approval.\n- The proposal currently says that no imagePullSecrets are used because both images are public. If role images go to a private registry, that statement and the chart both need to change.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2624,"cache_read_input_tokens":12729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2624},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a35fa2b5-d93b-4d8a-8dfa-4624f696edc9","uuid":"78f0482f-cb61-498f-a12d-e79b7374e072","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:47:08.406Z","request_id":"req_011ChQJTkwJ33jmcCerpMtcb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X5gnmjKEfWcLXnpiWZiwhT","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /work/.ard/245/triage-lead.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a35fa2b5-d93b-4d8a-8dfa-4624f696edc9","uuid":"95bc6a61-87bd-4124-84d1-4d627186fd88","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:47:08.422Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/work/.ard/245/triage-lead.md","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis is the last slice of the default agent image work. It lets roles that ship their own Dockerfile run under the Kubernetes executor by building those images and making them pullable by the cluster. Both dependencies appear to have landed on main: the local ard-agent image (part 55a) and the Kubernetes executor series, including its agent and pod images and image pins. So the work can start, and the engineer plans it.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: choose how role images build on the published agent image instead of the local-only one, where they are built and pushed, how the k8s executor picks the image for each role, and the tests and proposal update.\n- worker engineer: executor, build and docs changes, with tests.\n\n## Open issues\n- The repository has no architect triage role, so the engineer's plan has to make the design choices itself. These are: the base image for role images on the cluster path, the registry and whether it is public, and whether role images are built in CI and pinned by digest or built at runtime. A maintainer should check these choices in the plan before the worker starts.\n- The change will probably touch Jenkinsfile, Dockerfile or deploy/. Those are protected paths, so the pull request will wait for a human approval.\n- The proposal currently says that no imagePullSecrets are used because both images are public. If role images go to a private registry, that statement and the chart both need to change.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X5gnmjKEfWcLXnpiWZiwhT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQJURn9eb9shUC2oNgBw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #245 as ready to start. The engineer triage role will write the plan and the engineer worker will implement it. The decision is written to `.ard/245/triage-lead.md`.\n\n**Status:** done, with `next: [triage:engineer]` and `worker: engineer`.\n\n**Why it isn't blocked:** the issue depends on #54 and #243, and the git history suggests both are done:\n- #243 (the local ard-agent image) was merged as #324.\n- The Kubernetes executor has been merged in parts, up to the pod images (#320), the kind end-to-end test (#321) and the controller credential for the k8s executor (#439).\n\n**Why only the engineer:** the only triage role besides lead is engineer. The eng-review reviewer has no `when:` rule in the config, so it will review the pull request anyway and needs no `review:` entry.\n\n**What a maintainer should know** (also listed in the file's \"Open issues\" section):\n- **No architect role exists**, so the engineer's plan will make the design choices itself. These are: which base image role images build on in the cluster, which registry they go to and whether it's public, and whether they're built in CI and pinned by digest or built at runtime. Check these in the plan before the worker starts.\n- **The pull request will need human approval.** The change will probably touch `Jenkinsfile`, `Dockerfile` or `deploy/`, which are protected paths in `.ard/config.yaml`.\n- **The proposal says no image pull secrets are used** because both images are public. If role images go to a private registry, that statement and the chart both need to change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":987,"cache_read_input_tokens":15353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":987},"output_